{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01T3TtkeHhNAJZKXwkFTmNCH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_012xinWFsdPnoxwdALhuwTqE","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write payments-system-system-design-interview.html","prompt":"Write a complete HTML file at:\n`/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/payments-system-system-design-interview.html`\n\n## Goal\nA full 45–60 minute frontend system design interview answer for \"Design a Payments / Checkout Frontend\" (think Stripe, Braintree, PayPal).\n\n## Structure (5 collapsible sections, same as reference)\n① Requirements (5–10m)\n② Architecture (10–15m)  \n③ Data Model (~5m)\n④ API Design / BFF (~10m)\n⑤ Deep Dive (~10m) — tabbed panel with: Security, Performance, Observability, Resilience, i18n\n\n## Reference file to copy HTML skeleton / CSS / JS from:\n`/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/claude/claude-system-design-interview.html`\n\nRead that file first — copy its exact CSS variables, layout classes (section-block, section-head, section-num, deep-tabs, entity, component-tree, state-ladder, mermaid-wrap, checklist, callout, grid-2, card), JavaScript (mermaid init, collapse, deep tabs, checklist persistence, nav observer), and nav structure. Just change the content.\n\n## Content to write (payments-specific)\n\n### ① Requirements\n- Opening callout: \"Before I draw boxes, let me confirm what we're building and what we're NOT building in v1.\"\n- Functional requirements table (columns: Area | Must have (v1) | Nice to have):\n  - Checkout Form: multi-step flow (cart→shipping→payment→confirmation), card input with masking/BIN detection, address autocomplete | saved payment methods, buy-now-pay-later\n  - Security: Stripe Elements hosted fields, PCI SAQ-A scope | custom card form (SAQ-D — out of scope)\n  - Payment Methods: card (Visa/MC/Amex), basic wallets (Apple/Google Pay) | iDEAL, BLIK, Pix, UPI, BNPL\n  - Real-time: payment status polling / SSE after confirmation | live transaction dashboard\n  - Errors: decline handling, 3DS challenge, retry UX | full circuit breaker / provider failover\n\n- Non-functional grid-2 cards:\n  - Latency: checkout page LCP < 2.5s; form TTI < 3s on 4G; confirmCardPayment TTFB < 1s\n  - Scale: handle 10k concurrent checkout sessions; multi-tab same cart\n  - Reliability: idempotency for all payment mutations; offline queue for pre-auth steps; webhook-to-UI reconciliation\n  - Security: PCI SAQ-A via hosted fields; CSP with Stripe allowlist; no raw PAN/CVV in browser memory\n\n- Metrics · Constraints · Assumptions bullet list:\n  - Metrics: checkout conversion rate, payment success rate by decline code, 3DS completion rate, Stripe.js load time p95\n  - Constraints: raw card data NEVER touches our DOM/server (only Stripe iframe); Stripe.js must load on every page; mobile Safari SSE limits\n  - Assumptions: Stripe as primary PSP; single-currency v1; authenticated sessions; BFF owns Stripe secret key\n\n- Scoping checklist (checkboxes):\n  - Multi-PSP routing needed in v1?\n  - Saved payment methods (returning user flow)?\n  - Local payment methods (iDEAL, BLIK, etc.)?\n  - Offline resilience required?\n  - Multi-currency marketplace?\n\n- Section links: § answers-html/01-checkout-flow-form-ux.html and answers-html/02-payment-security-pci-compliance.html\n\n### ② Architecture\n- Stack: React 18 + TypeScript · XState for payment FSM · React Query for cart/session · Vite build · SSE for payment status · Stripe Elements for card input\n- Mermaid flowchart (TB):\n  ```\n  subgraph UI Layer: CheckoutShell, StepRouter, CardForm (Stripe Elements), OrderSummary, ConfirmationPage\n  subgraph Client State: PaymentFSM (XState), CartStore, SessionStore (idempotency keys), OptimisticLayer\n  subgraph Transport: REST/HTTPS control plane, SSE payment status, postMessage (Stripe iframe ↔ parent)\n  subgraph BFF / API: Checkout API, PaymentIntent Service, Webhook Receiver, PSP Adapter\n  subgraph External: Stripe API, Stripe.js CDN, Payment Methods (Apple/Google Pay)\n  subgraph Persistence: Postgres (orders/users), Redis (session/idempotency), sessionStorage (form draft)\n  ```\n  Edges: CardForm --postMessage--> Stripe iframe, UI --REST--> BFF, SSE --status push--> PaymentFSM, Webhook --verified--> DB, BFF --idempotency--> Redis\n\n- Component tree (mermaid flowchart):\n  ```\n  AppShell → CheckoutLayout, GlobalProviders\n  CheckoutLayout → StepRouter, OrderSummarySidebar, ProgressIndicator\n  StepRouter → CartStep, ShippingStep, PaymentStep, ConfirmationStep\n  PaymentStep → StripeElementsProvider, CardInputFrame (Stripe iframe), PaymentMethodSelector, WalletButtons (Apple/Google Pay), PayNowButton, ErrorDisplay, ThreeDSModal\n  StripeElementsProvider → CardNumberElement, CardExpiryElement, CardCvcElement\n  GlobalProviders → AuthProvider, StripeProvider, QueryClientProvider, BroadcastChannel\n  ```\n\n- State management ladder:\n  - Ephemeral (JS): card input state (inside Stripe iframe, never in our JS), rAF animation queue, BIN detection result\n  - sessionStorage: multi-step form progress, idempotency key per attempt, cart snapshot for recovery\n  - React Query cache: cart data, user session, order summary\n  - XState machine: PaymentIntent FSM (requires_payment_method → requires_action → processing → succeeded)\n  - Server SoT: PaymentIntent object, Order record, Webhook event log\n\n- Callout: \"Card data NEVER enters our React state or memory — it lives exclusively in the Stripe cross-origin iframe. Our state machine only tracks PaymentIntent status strings.\"\n\n- Section links to answers-html/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.html and answers-html/09-architecture-provider-abstraction.html\n\n### ③ Data Model\n- Prose: \"Frontend operates on three core entities: the Cart (ephemeral), the CheckoutSession (server-persisted), and the PaymentIntent (Stripe-owned). We never model raw card data.\"\n- Entity block (monospace pre):\n```\nCart {\n  id, items: LineItem[], subtotal, currency,\n  appliedCoupons: Coupon[],\n  expiresAt  // server-side cart TTL\n}\n\nCheckoutSession {\n  id, cartId, userId?,\n  step: 'cart' | 'shipping' | 'payment' | 'confirmation',\n  shippingAddress: Address,\n  selectedPaymentMethodId?,\n  idempotencyKey,    // per-attempt, rotated on each \"Pay\" click\n  createdAt, updatedAt\n}\n\nPaymentIntent {               // Stripe-owned, mirrored to our DB\n  id: 'pi_xxx',\n  amount, currency,\n  status: PIStatus,           // FSM state\n  clientSecret,               // short-lived, never stored in localStorage\n  paymentMethodId?,\n  lastPaymentError?: StripeError,\n  nextAction?: NextAction     // 3DS redirect / iframe challenge\n}\n\nOrder {\n  id, paymentIntentId, userId, items,\n  status: 'pending' | 'paid' | 'failed' | 'refunded',\n  paidAt?, webhookVerifiedAt\n}\n\ntype PIStatus = \n  | 'requires_payment_method'\n  | 'requires_confirmation'\n  | 'requires_action'\n  | 'processing'\n  | 'succeeded'\n  | 'canceled'\n```\n\n- Key relationships table (Operation | Behavior):\n  - User clicks Pay | POST /payment-intents/confirm → Stripe confirmCardPayment → PI status → processing\n  - 3DS required | PI nextAction triggers ThreeDSModal mount; on complete → PI → succeeded\n  - Webhook arrives | DB Order.status = 'paid'; SSE pushes to active frontend session\n  - Tab re-entry after close | GET /checkout-session → restore step + PI status; re-render correct UI\n  - Card decline | PI.lastPaymentError populated; FSM → requires_payment_method; user can retry\n\n- Section links to answers-html/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.html and answers-html/04-real-time-updates-webhooks.html\n\n### ④ API Design / BFF\n- Protocol choice table (Pattern | Use in payments | Why):\n  - REST/HTTPS | Cart CRUD, session management, PaymentIntent confirm, order fetch | Idempotency-Key header; standard error taxonomy; caching for GET\n  - SSE | Payment status push after confirmation | Server→client push; no polling; AbortController cancel; works with standard auth cookies\n  - postMessage | Stripe Elements iframe → parent page | Cross-origin card data isolation — PCI requirement\n  - WebSocket | Live dashboard (multi-concurrent payments) | Full-duplex for high-frequency event push; not needed for single-session checkout\n  - Polling (fallback) | Payment status if SSE unavailable | Exponential backoff; safe fallback for restrictive network proxies\n\n- Core endpoints table (Method | Endpoint | Purpose):\n  - POST | /checkout/session | Create or resume CheckoutSession; returns sessionId + step\n  - PATCH | /checkout/session/:id/step | Advance to next step (validates current step server-side)\n  - POST | /payment-intents | Create PI server-side; returns clientSecret (never stored, used once)\n  - POST | /payment-intents/:id/confirm | Trigger confirmCardPayment; idempotent via Idempotency-Key\n  - GET | /payment-intents/:id/status | Poll fallback for PI status\n  - GET | /payment-status-stream?piId=:id | SSE stream for real-time PI status updates\n  - POST | /webhooks/stripe | Verify Stripe-Signature; update Order; push to SSE clients\n  - GET | /orders/:id | Confirmation page data fetch\n\n- Streaming / async lifecycle:\n  ```\n  User clicks Pay →\n    [1] POST /payment-intents/confirm (Idempotency-Key: session.idempotencyKey)\n    [2] BFF calls stripe.paymentIntents.confirm()\n    [3] If 3DS required: return nextAction to frontend → render ThreeDSModal\n    [4] After 3DS: PI status = processing → SSE pushes update\n    [5] Stripe webhook → BFF verifies sig → updates Order → SSE broadcast → UI → ConfirmationPage\n  ```\n\n- Network lifecycle notes:\n  - Idempotency: rotate key per attempt; safe to retry POST on timeout without double-charge\n  - Cancel: if user navigates away during processing, Order status resolved by webhook (frontend re-reads on return)\n  - 3DS redirect recovery: store PI id in sessionStorage before redirect; restore on return\n  - Backoff: poll fallback at 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s (cap 30s); show \"still processing...\" after 10s\n\n- Section links to answers-html/04-real-time-updates-webhooks.html and answers-html/06-error-handling-resilience.html\n\n### ⑤ Deep Dive — 5 tabs\nOpening line (in prose): \"I'll lead with Security (PCI/iframe model) and Resilience — happy to switch to Performance or i18n if you prefer.\"\n\n**Tab: Security** (id=\"panel-sec\", active by default)\n- PCI scope: Stripe Elements = SAQ-A; card data never in our DOM, memory, or server logs\n- iframe isolation: Stripe renders CardNumberElement in cross-origin iframe on js.stripe.com; postMessage only exchanges tokens (pm_xxx), never PANs\n- CSP: `frame-src https://js.stripe.com https://hooks.stripe.com; script-src 'self' https://js.stripe.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.stripe.com`\n- clientSecret: keep in memory only (not localStorage, not URL params); expires after PI use; rotate idempotency key per attempt\n- Clickjacking: X-Frame-Options DENY on checkout page + frame-ancestors 'none' in CSP; Stripe iframe is explicitly allowed via frame-src, not by weakening our own page framing policy\n- 3DS: iframe modal challenge or redirect; validate redirect return params server-side via webhook; never trust client-side redirect_status alone\n\n**Tab: Performance** (id=\"panel-perf\")\n- Stripe.js: load on every page (Stripe recommends this for fraud signals); use &lt;script async&gt; + preconnect to js.stripe.com\n- CLS prevention: reserve fixed height (e.g. 48px) for Elements iframe mount container; don't let it reflow surrounding content\n- Bundle split: core checkout critical path is &lt;60KB; defer Stripe.js (already async); lazy-load Apple/Google Pay button SDKs only when available\n- TBT: move heavy Stripe SDK work off main thread by loading async; INP-safe by debouncing BIN detection to 300ms\n- One-click checkout: preload PI on product page hover/intent; preconnect Stripe on page load; so that \"Pay\" click triggers confirm only, not create+confirm\n- LCP: inline critical CSS; preload hero product image; SSR order summary so content is above-fold on first byte\n\n**Tab: Resilience** (id=\"panel-res\")\n- Idempotency: every POST /payment-intents/confirm carries Idempotency-Key from sessionStorage; safe to retry on network timeout\n- 3DS redirect recovery: stash PI id + step in sessionStorage before redirect; restore on return to correct UI state\n- Offline detection: navigator.onLine + online/offline events; show \"you're offline, your cart is saved\" banner; queue retry on reconnect\n- Webhook ground truth: never trust only client-side PI status; always wait for webhook-confirmed Order.status before showing success\n- Circuit breaker: after 3 consecutive 5xx from /payment-intents/confirm in 60s, show \"payment system temporarily unavailable\" with retry-after countdown; don't let user hammer degraded backend\n- Tab re-entry: GET /checkout-session on tab focus to reconcile FSM state with server PI status; BroadcastChannel for multi-tab same cart conflict detection\n\n**Tab: Observability** (id=\"panel-obs\")\n- Funnel events: checkout_started, step_completed (step, duration_ms), payment_form_engaged, pay_button_clicked, payment_succeeded / payment_failed (decline_code, attempt_number)\n- PCI-safe sanitization: Sentry beforeSend strips card_number, cvv, full_name from breadcrumbs; analytics allowlist only (pi_id hashed, decline_code, country)\n- Performance marks: performance.mark('stripe-js-start') before script inject → performance.mark('stripe-js-ready') in Stripe onReady callback; performance.mark('elements-mounted') in Elements onChange\n- Real-time dashboard: payment_success_rate (1m rolling window), decline_rate by code, 3DS completion %, Stripe.js p95 load time; alert if success_rate &lt; 90% for 5 min\n- Deploy regression: correlate deploy timestamp with Sentry error spike and Datadog payment_failed rate; cross-check Stripe Dashboard for PSP-side failures vs. our API errors\n\n**Tab: i18n** (id=\"panel-i18n\")\n- Currency formatting: Intl.NumberFormat(locale, {style:'currency', currency}) for display; always store/transmit in minor units (integer cents); special-case JPY (0 decimals), KWD (3 decimals)\n- Tax display: server provides {amount, taxIncluded: boolean, taxAmount}; component renders \"incl. VAT\" or \"+ tax\" based on flag; never derive tax from frontend\n- RTL: CSS logical properties (margin-inline-start not margin-left); card number field kept LTR via dir=\"ltr\" on the input; CVV icon flips position; error messages align-start\n- Local payment methods: server returns ranked PaymentMethod[] for locale; frontend renders in server order; each method has {type, displayName, logoUrl, flow: 'redirect'|'iframe'|'async'}; iDEAL/BLIK are redirect; Pix/UPI are async (polling for QR scan); konbini is async + shows convenience store selector\n- Server error translation: decline codes mapped to i18n key in frontend dictionary; fallback to generic \"payment_failed\" if code unknown; never show raw PSP error strings to users\n\n### Interview close (30 sec)\ncallout: \"Three patterns I'd repeat: (1) card data stays in Stripe's iframe — scope our PCI to SAQ-A and never touch raw PANs; (2) idempotency keys + webhook ground truth — rotate per attempt, never trust client-side confirmCardPayment alone; (3) PaymentIntent as FSM — model status transitions explicitly so every UI state is deterministic and recoverable.\"\n\n- Section links: answers-html/06-error-handling-resilience.html, answers-html/02-payment-security-pci-compliance.html, answers-html/08-observability-analytics.html\n\n## Nav and footer links\n- Nav title: \"Payments SD — Interview\"\n- Nav links: #requirements #architecture #data-model #api-design #deep-dive\n- Top-right links: href=\"../payments-system-frontend-architecture.html\" and href=\"answers-html/index.html\"\n- Footer: links to answers-html/index.html, payments-system-frontend-architecture.html, payments-system-design-doc.md\n\n## HTML rules\n- NO data-demo panels\n- Mermaid: startOnLoad: false; lazy render via mermaid.run()\n- Deep tabs default: Security active (not Performance like in the reference)\n- Checklist persistence via localStorage (same pattern as reference)\n- Copy exact JS for collapse, nav observer, deep tabs, checklist from reference file\n\nWrite the full HTML file now. It should be self-contained, ~700-900 lines, match the reference's visual style exactly."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19330,"cache_read_input_tokens":36515,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":19330,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f24c5cdf-0369-4a81-99d5-ba16ab3babb1","uuid":"39e16c47-b77c-4031-b053-7acf6d53baad"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a7b7ab323c2033781","tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_012xinWFsdPnoxwdALhuwTqE","description":"Write payments-system-system-design-interview.html","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Write a complete HTML file at:\n`/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/payments-system-system-design-interview.html`\n\n## Goal\nA full 45–60 minute frontend system design interview answer for \"Design a Payments / Checkout Frontend\" (think Stripe, Braintree, PayPal).\n\n## Structure (5 collapsible sections, same as reference)\n① Requirements (5–10m)\n② Architecture (10–15m)  \n③ Data Model (~5m)\n④ API Design / BFF (~10m)\n⑤ Deep Dive (~10m) — tabbed panel with: Security, Performance, Observability, Resilience, i18n\n\n## Reference file to copy HTML skeleton / CSS / JS from:\n`/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/claude/claude-system-design-interview.html`\n\nRead that file first — copy its exact CSS variables, layout classes (section-block, section-head, section-num, deep-tabs, entity, component-tree, state-ladder, mermaid-wrap, checklist, callout, grid-2, card), JavaScript (mermaid init, collapse, deep tabs, checklist persistence, nav observer), and nav structure. Just change the content.\n\n## Content to write (payments-specific)\n\n### ① Requirements\n- Opening callout: \"Before I draw boxes, let me confirm what we're building and what we're NOT building in v1.\"\n- Functional requirements table (columns: Area | Must have (v1) | Nice to have):\n  - Checkout Form: multi-step flow (cart→shipping→payment→confirmation), card input with masking/BIN detection, address autocomplete | saved payment methods, buy-now-pay-later\n  - Security: Stripe Elements hosted fields, PCI SAQ-A scope | custom card form (SAQ-D — out of scope)\n  - Payment Methods: card (Visa/MC/Amex), basic wallets (Apple/Google Pay) | iDEAL, BLIK, Pix, UPI, BNPL\n  - Real-time: payment status polling / SSE after confirmation | live transaction dashboard\n  - Errors: decline handling, 3DS challenge, retry UX | full circuit breaker / provider failover\n\n- Non-functional grid-2 cards:\n  - Latency: checkout page LCP < 2.5s; form TTI < 3s on 4G; confirmCardPayment TTFB < 1s\n  - Scale: handle 10k concurrent checkout sessions; multi-tab same cart\n  - Reliability: idempotency for all payment mutations; offline queue for pre-auth steps; webhook-to-UI reconciliation\n  - Security: PCI SAQ-A via hosted fields; CSP with Stripe allowlist; no raw PAN/CVV in browser memory\n\n- Metrics · Constraints · Assumptions bullet list:\n  - Metrics: checkout conversion rate, payment success rate by decline code, 3DS completion rate, Stripe.js load time p95\n  - Constraints: raw card data NEVER touches our DOM/server (only Stripe iframe); Stripe.js must load on every page; mobile Safari SSE limits\n  - Assumptions: Stripe as primary PSP; single-currency v1; authenticated sessions; BFF owns Stripe secret key\n\n- Scoping checklist (checkboxes):\n  - Multi-PSP routing needed in v1?\n  - Saved payment methods (returning user flow)?\n  - Local payment methods (iDEAL, BLIK, etc.)?\n  - Offline resilience required?\n  - Multi-currency marketplace?\n\n- Section links: § answers-html/01-checkout-flow-form-ux.html and answers-html/02-payment-security-pci-compliance.html\n\n### ② Architecture\n- Stack: React 18 + TypeScript · XState for payment FSM · React Query for cart/session · Vite build · SSE for payment status · Stripe Elements for card input\n- Mermaid flowchart (TB):\n  ```\n  subgraph UI Layer: CheckoutShell, StepRouter, CardForm (Stripe Elements), OrderSummary, ConfirmationPage\n  subgraph Client State: PaymentFSM (XState), CartStore, SessionStore (idempotency keys), OptimisticLayer\n  subgraph Transport: REST/HTTPS control plane, SSE payment status, postMessage (Stripe iframe ↔ parent)\n  subgraph BFF / API: Checkout API, PaymentIntent Service, Webhook Receiver, PSP Adapter\n  subgraph External: Stripe API, Stripe.js CDN, Payment Methods (Apple/Google Pay)\n  subgraph Persistence: Postgres (orders/users), Redis (session/idempotency), sessionStorage (form draft)\n  ```\n  Edges: CardForm --postMessage--> Stripe iframe, UI --REST--> BFF, SSE --status push--> PaymentFSM, Webhook --verified--> DB, BFF --idempotency--> Redis\n\n- Component tree (mermaid flowchart):\n  ```\n  AppShell → CheckoutLayout, GlobalProviders\n  CheckoutLayout → StepRouter, OrderSummarySidebar, ProgressIndicator\n  StepRouter → CartStep, ShippingStep, PaymentStep, ConfirmationStep\n  PaymentStep → StripeElementsProvider, CardInputFrame (Stripe iframe), PaymentMethodSelector, WalletButtons (Apple/Google Pay), PayNowButton, ErrorDisplay, ThreeDSModal\n  StripeElementsProvider → CardNumberElement, CardExpiryElement, CardCvcElement\n  GlobalProviders → AuthProvider, StripeProvider, QueryClientProvider, BroadcastChannel\n  ```\n\n- State management ladder:\n  - Ephemeral (JS): card input state (inside Stripe iframe, never in our JS), rAF animation queue, BIN detection result\n  - sessionStorage: multi-step form progress, idempotency key per attempt, cart snapshot for recovery\n  - React Query cache: cart data, user session, order summary\n  - XState machine: PaymentIntent FSM (requires_payment_method → requires_action → processing → succeeded)\n  - Server SoT: PaymentIntent object, Order record, Webhook event log\n\n- Callout: \"Card data NEVER enters our React state or memory — it lives exclusively in the Stripe cross-origin iframe. Our state machine only tracks PaymentIntent status strings.\"\n\n- Section links to answers-html/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.html and answers-html/09-architecture-provider-abstraction.html\n\n### ③ Data Model\n- Prose: \"Frontend operates on three core entities: the Cart (ephemeral), the CheckoutSession (server-persisted), and the PaymentIntent (Stripe-owned). We never model raw card data.\"\n- Entity block (monospace pre):\n```\nCart {\n  id, items: LineItem[], subtotal, currency,\n  appliedCoupons: Coupon[],\n  expiresAt  // server-side cart TTL\n}\n\nCheckoutSession {\n  id, cartId, userId?,\n  step: 'cart' | 'shipping' | 'payment' | 'confirmation',\n  shippingAddress: Address,\n  selectedPaymentMethodId?,\n  idempotencyKey,    // per-attempt, rotated on each \"Pay\" click\n  createdAt, updatedAt\n}\n\nPaymentIntent {               // Stripe-owned, mirrored to our DB\n  id: 'pi_xxx',\n  amount, currency,\n  status: PIStatus,           // FSM state\n  clientSecret,               // short-lived, never stored in localStorage\n  paymentMethodId?,\n  lastPaymentError?: StripeError,\n  nextAction?: NextAction     // 3DS redirect / iframe challenge\n}\n\nOrder {\n  id, paymentIntentId, userId, items,\n  status: 'pending' | 'paid' | 'failed' | 'refunded',\n  paidAt?, webhookVerifiedAt\n}\n\ntype PIStatus = \n  | 'requires_payment_method'\n  | 'requires_confirmation'\n  | 'requires_action'\n  | 'processing'\n  | 'succeeded'\n  | 'canceled'\n```\n\n- Key relationships table (Operation | Behavior):\n  - User clicks Pay | POST /payment-intents/confirm → Stripe confirmCardPayment → PI status → processing\n  - 3DS required | PI nextAction triggers ThreeDSModal mount; on complete → PI → succeeded\n  - Webhook arrives | DB Order.status = 'paid'; SSE pushes to active frontend session\n  - Tab re-entry after close | GET /checkout-session → restore step + PI status; re-render correct UI\n  - Card decline | PI.lastPaymentError populated; FSM → requires_payment_method; user can retry\n\n- Section links to answers-html/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.html and answers-html/04-real-time-updates-webhooks.html\n\n### ④ API Design / BFF\n- Protocol choice table (Pattern | Use in payments | Why):\n  - REST/HTTPS | Cart CRUD, session management, PaymentIntent confirm, order fetch | Idempotency-Key header; standard error taxonomy; caching for GET\n  - SSE | Payment status push after confirmation | Server→client push; no polling; AbortController cancel; works with standard auth cookies\n  - postMessage | Stripe Elements iframe → parent page | Cross-origin card data isolation — PCI requirement\n  - WebSocket | Live dashboard (multi-concurrent payments) | Full-duplex for high-frequency event push; not needed for single-session checkout\n  - Polling (fallback) | Payment status if SSE unavailable | Exponential backoff; safe fallback for restrictive network proxies\n\n- Core endpoints table (Method | Endpoint | Purpose):\n  - POST | /checkout/session | Create or resume CheckoutSession; returns sessionId + step\n  - PATCH | /checkout/session/:id/step | Advance to next step (validates current step server-side)\n  - POST | /payment-intents | Create PI server-side; returns clientSecret (never stored, used once)\n  - POST | /payment-intents/:id/confirm | Trigger confirmCardPayment; idempotent via Idempotency-Key\n  - GET | /payment-intents/:id/status | Poll fallback for PI status\n  - GET | /payment-status-stream?piId=:id | SSE stream for real-time PI status updates\n  - POST | /webhooks/stripe | Verify Stripe-Signature; update Order; push to SSE clients\n  - GET | /orders/:id | Confirmation page data fetch\n\n- Streaming / async lifecycle:\n  ```\n  User clicks Pay →\n    [1] POST /payment-intents/confirm (Idempotency-Key: session.idempotencyKey)\n    [2] BFF calls stripe.paymentIntents.confirm()\n    [3] If 3DS required: return nextAction to frontend → render ThreeDSModal\n    [4] After 3DS: PI status = processing → SSE pushes update\n    [5] Stripe webhook → BFF verifies sig → updates Order → SSE broadcast → UI → ConfirmationPage\n  ```\n\n- Network lifecycle notes:\n  - Idempotency: rotate key per attempt; safe to retry POST on timeout without double-charge\n  - Cancel: if user navigates away during processing, Order status resolved by webhook (frontend re-reads on return)\n  - 3DS redirect recovery: store PI id in sessionStorage before redirect; restore on return\n  - Backoff: poll fallback at 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s (cap 30s); show \"still processing...\" after 10s\n\n- Section links to answers-html/04-real-time-updates-webhooks.html and answers-html/06-error-handling-resilience.html\n\n### ⑤ Deep Dive — 5 tabs\nOpening line (in prose): \"I'll lead with Security (PCI/iframe model) and Resilience — happy to switch to Performance or i18n if you prefer.\"\n\n**Tab: Security** (id=\"panel-sec\", active by default)\n- PCI scope: Stripe Elements = SAQ-A; card data never in our DOM, memory, or server logs\n- iframe isolation: Stripe renders CardNumberElement in cross-origin iframe on js.stripe.com; postMessage only exchanges tokens (pm_xxx), never PANs\n- CSP: `frame-src https://js.stripe.com https://hooks.stripe.com; script-src 'self' https://js.stripe.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.stripe.com`\n- clientSecret: keep in memory only (not localStorage, not URL params); expires after PI use; rotate idempotency key per attempt\n- Clickjacking: X-Frame-Options DENY on checkout page + frame-ancestors 'none' in CSP; Stripe iframe is explicitly allowed via frame-src, not by weakening our own page framing policy\n- 3DS: iframe modal challenge or redirect; validate redirect return params server-side via webhook; never trust client-side redirect_status alone\n\n**Tab: Performance** (id=\"panel-perf\")\n- Stripe.js: load on every page (Stripe recommends this for fraud signals); use &lt;script async&gt; + preconnect to js.stripe.com\n- CLS prevention: reserve fixed height (e.g. 48px) for Elements iframe mount container; don't let it reflow surrounding content\n- Bundle split: core checkout critical path is &lt;60KB; defer Stripe.js (already async); lazy-load Apple/Google Pay button SDKs only when available\n- TBT: move heavy Stripe SDK work off main thread by loading async; INP-safe by debouncing BIN detection to 300ms\n- One-click checkout: preload PI on product page hover/intent; preconnect Stripe on page load; so that \"Pay\" click triggers confirm only, not create+confirm\n- LCP: inline critical CSS; preload hero product image; SSR order summary so content is above-fold on first byte\n\n**Tab: Resilience** (id=\"panel-res\")\n- Idempotency: every POST /payment-intents/confirm carries Idempotency-Key from sessionStorage; safe to retry on network timeout\n- 3DS redirect recovery: stash PI id + step in sessionStorage before redirect; restore on return to correct UI state\n- Offline detection: navigator.onLine + online/offline events; show \"you're offline, your cart is saved\" banner; queue retry on reconnect\n- Webhook ground truth: never trust only client-side PI status; always wait for webhook-confirmed Order.status before showing success\n- Circuit breaker: after 3 consecutive 5xx from /payment-intents/confirm in 60s, show \"payment system temporarily unavailable\" with retry-after countdown; don't let user hammer degraded backend\n- Tab re-entry: GET /checkout-session on tab focus to reconcile FSM state with server PI status; BroadcastChannel for multi-tab same cart conflict detection\n\n**Tab: Observability** (id=\"panel-obs\")\n- Funnel events: checkout_started, step_completed (step, duration_ms), payment_form_engaged, pay_button_clicked, payment_succeeded / payment_failed (decline_code, attempt_number)\n- PCI-safe sanitization: Sentry beforeSend strips card_number, cvv, full_name from breadcrumbs; analytics allowlist only (pi_id hashed, decline_code, country)\n- Performance marks: performance.mark('stripe-js-start') before script inject → performance.mark('stripe-js-ready') in Stripe onReady callback; performance.mark('elements-mounted') in Elements onChange\n- Real-time dashboard: payment_success_rate (1m rolling window), decline_rate by code, 3DS completion %, Stripe.js p95 load time; alert if success_rate &lt; 90% for 5 min\n- Deploy regression: correlate deploy timestamp with Sentry error spike and Datadog payment_failed rate; cross-check Stripe Dashboard for PSP-side failures vs. our API errors\n\n**Tab: i18n** (id=\"panel-i18n\")\n- Currency formatting: Intl.NumberFormat(locale, {style:'currency', currency}) for display; always store/transmit in minor units (integer cents); special-case JPY (0 decimals), KWD (3 decimals)\n- Tax display: server provides {amount, taxIncluded: boolean, taxAmount}; component renders \"incl. VAT\" or \"+ tax\" based on flag; never derive tax from frontend\n- RTL: CSS logical properties (margin-inline-start not margin-left); card number field kept LTR via dir=\"ltr\" on the input; CVV icon flips position; error messages align-start\n- Local payment methods: server returns ranked PaymentMethod[] for locale; frontend renders in server order; each method has {type, displayName, logoUrl, flow: 'redirect'|'iframe'|'async'}; iDEAL/BLIK are redirect; Pix/UPI are async (polling for QR scan); konbini is async + shows convenience store selector\n- Server error translation: decline codes mapped to i18n key in frontend dictionary; fallback to generic \"payment_failed\" if code unknown; never show raw PSP error strings to users\n\n### Interview close (30 sec)\ncallout: \"Three patterns I'd repeat: (1) card data stays in Stripe's iframe — scope our PCI to SAQ-A and never touch raw PANs; (2) idempotency keys + webhook ground truth — rotate per attempt, never trust client-side confirmCardPayment alone; (3) PaymentIntent as FSM — model status transitions explicitly so every UI state is deterministic and recoverable.\"\n\n- Section links: answers-html/06-error-handling-resilience.html, answers-html/02-payment-security-pci-compliance.html, answers-html/08-observability-analytics.html\n\n## Nav and footer links\n- Nav title: \"Payments SD — Interview\"\n- Nav links: #requirements #architecture #data-model #api-design #deep-dive\n- Top-right links: href=\"../payments-system-frontend-architecture.html\" and href=\"answers-html/index.html\"\n- Footer: links to answers-html/index.html, payments-system-frontend-architecture.html, payments-system-design-doc.md\n\n## HTML rules\n- NO data-demo panels\n- Mermaid: startOnLoad: false; lazy render via mermaid.run()\n- Deep tabs default: Security active (not Performance like in the reference)\n- Checklist persistence via localStorage (same pattern as reference)\n- Copy exact JS for collapse, nav observer, deep tabs, checklist from reference file\n\nWrite the full HTML file now. It should be self-contained, ~700-900 lines, match the reference's visual style exactly.","uuid":"12d1116a-f83e-45e1-a510-0c7e04fff39b","session_id":"f24c5cdf-0369-4a81-99d5-ba16ab3babb1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Write a complete HTML file at:\n`/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/payments-system-system-design-interview.html`\n\n## Goal\nA full 45–60 minute frontend system design interview answer for \"Design a Payments / Checkout Frontend\" (think Stripe, Braintree, PayPal).\n\n## Structure (5 collapsible sections, same as reference)\n① Requirements (5–10m)\n② Architecture (10–15m)  \n③ Data Model (~5m)\n④ API Design / BFF (~10m)\n⑤ Deep Dive (~10m) — tabbed panel with: Security, Performance, Observability, Resilience, i18n\n\n## Reference file to copy HTML skeleton / CSS / JS from:\n`/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/claude/claude-system-design-interview.html`\n\nRead that file first — copy its exact CSS variables, layout classes (section-block, section-head, section-num, deep-tabs, entity, component-tree, state-ladder, mermaid-wrap, checklist, callout, grid-2, card), JavaScript (mermaid init, collapse, deep tabs, checklist persistence, nav observer), and nav structure. Just change the content.\n\n## Content to write (payments-specific)\n\n### ① Requirements\n- Opening callout: \"Before I draw boxes, let me confirm what we're building and what we're NOT building in v1.\"\n- Functional requirements table (columns: Area | Must have (v1) | Nice to have):\n  - Checkout Form: multi-step flow (cart→shipping→payment→confirmation), card input with masking/BIN detection, address autocomplete | saved payment methods, buy-now-pay-later\n  - Security: Stripe Elements hosted fields, PCI SAQ-A scope | custom card form (SAQ-D — out of scope)\n  - Payment Methods: card (Visa/MC/Amex), basic wallets (Apple/Google Pay) | iDEAL, BLIK, Pix, UPI, BNPL\n  - Real-time: payment status polling / SSE after confirmation | live transaction dashboard\n  - Errors: decline handling, 3DS challenge, retry UX | full circuit breaker / provider failover\n\n- Non-functional grid-2 cards:\n  - Latency: checkout page LCP < 2.5s; form TTI < 3s on 4G; confirmCardPayment TTFB < 1s\n  - Scale: handle 10k concurrent checkout sessions; multi-tab same cart\n  - Reliability: idempotency for all payment mutations; offline queue for pre-auth steps; webhook-to-UI reconciliation\n  - Security: PCI SAQ-A via hosted fields; CSP with Stripe allowlist; no raw PAN/CVV in browser memory\n\n- Metrics · Constraints · Assumptions bullet list:\n  - Metrics: checkout conversion rate, payment success rate by decline code, 3DS completion rate, Stripe.js load time p95\n  - Constraints: raw card data NEVER touches our DOM/server (only Stripe iframe); Stripe.js must load on every page; mobile Safari SSE limits\n  - Assumptions: Stripe as primary PSP; single-currency v1; authenticated sessions; BFF owns Stripe secret key\n\n- Scoping checklist (checkboxes):\n  - Multi-PSP routing needed in v1?\n  - Saved payment methods (returning user flow)?\n  - Local payment methods (iDEAL, BLIK, etc.)?\n  - Offline resilience required?\n  - Multi-currency marketplace?\n\n- Section links: § answers-html/01-checkout-flow-form-ux.html and answers-html/02-payment-security-pci-compliance.html\n\n### ② Architecture\n- Stack: React 18 + TypeScript · XState for payment FSM · React Query for cart/session · Vite build · SSE for payment status · Stripe Elements for card input\n- Mermaid flowchart (TB):\n  ```\n  subgraph UI Layer: CheckoutShell, StepRouter, CardForm (Stripe Elements), OrderSummary, ConfirmationPage\n  subgraph Client State: PaymentFSM (XState), CartStore, SessionStore (idempotency keys), OptimisticLayer\n  subgraph Transport: REST/HTTPS control plane, SSE payment status, postMessage (Stripe iframe ↔ parent)\n  subgraph BFF / API: Checkout API, PaymentIntent Service, Webhook Receiver, PSP Adapter\n  subgraph External: Stripe API, Stripe.js CDN, Payment Methods (Apple/Google Pay)\n  subgraph Persistence: Postgres (orders/users), Redis (session/idempotency), sessionStorage (form draft)\n  ```\n  Edges: CardForm --postMessage--> Stripe iframe, UI --REST--> BFF, SSE --status push--> PaymentFSM, Webhook --verified--> DB, BFF --idempotency--> Redis\n\n- Component tree (mermaid flowchart):\n  ```\n  AppShell → CheckoutLayout, GlobalProviders\n  CheckoutLayout → StepRouter, OrderSummarySidebar, ProgressIndicator\n  StepRouter → CartStep, ShippingStep, PaymentStep, ConfirmationStep\n  PaymentStep → StripeElementsProvider, CardInputFrame (Stripe iframe), PaymentMethodSelector, WalletButtons (Apple/Google Pay), PayNowButton, ErrorDisplay, ThreeDSModal\n  StripeElementsProvider → CardNumberElement, CardExpiryElement, CardCvcElement\n  GlobalProviders → AuthProvider, StripeProvider, QueryClientProvider, BroadcastChannel\n  ```\n\n- State management ladder:\n  - Ephemeral (JS): card input state (inside Stripe iframe, never in our JS), rAF animation queue, BIN detection result\n  - sessionStorage: multi-step form progress, idempotency key per attempt, cart snapshot for recovery\n  - React Query cache: cart data, user session, order summary\n  - XState machine: PaymentIntent FSM (requires_payment_method → requires_action → processing → succeeded)\n  - Server SoT: PaymentIntent object, Order record, Webhook event log\n\n- Callout: \"Card data NEVER enters our React state or memory — it lives exclusively in the Stripe cross-origin iframe. Our state machine only tracks PaymentIntent status strings.\"\n\n- Section links to answers-html/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.html and answers-html/09-architecture-provider-abstraction.html\n\n### ③ Data Model\n- Prose: \"Frontend operates on three core entities: the Cart (ephemeral), the CheckoutSession (server-persisted), and the PaymentIntent (Stripe-owned). We never model raw card data.\"\n- Entity block (monospace pre):\n```\nCart {\n  id, items: LineItem[], subtotal, currency,\n  appliedCoupons: Coupon[],\n  expiresAt  // server-side cart TTL\n}\n\nCheckoutSession {\n  id, cartId, userId?,\n  step: 'cart' | 'shipping' | 'payment' | 'confirmation',\n  shippingAddress: Address,\n  selectedPaymentMethodId?,\n  idempotencyKey,    // per-attempt, rotated on each \"Pay\" click\n  createdAt, updatedAt\n}\n\nPaymentIntent {               // Stripe-owned, mirrored to our DB\n  id: 'pi_xxx',\n  amount, currency,\n  status: PIStatus,           // FSM state\n  clientSecret,               // short-lived, never stored in localStorage\n  paymentMethodId?,\n  lastPaymentError?: StripeError,\n  nextAction?: NextAction     // 3DS redirect / iframe challenge\n}\n\nOrder {\n  id, paymentIntentId, userId, items,\n  status: 'pending' | 'paid' | 'failed' | 'refunded',\n  paidAt?, webhookVerifiedAt\n}\n\ntype PIStatus = \n  | 'requires_payment_method'\n  | 'requires_confirmation'\n  | 'requires_action'\n  | 'processing'\n  | 'succeeded'\n  | 'canceled'\n```\n\n- Key relationships table (Operation | Behavior):\n  - User clicks Pay | POST /payment-intents/confirm → Stripe confirmCardPayment → PI status → processing\n  - 3DS required | PI nextAction triggers ThreeDSModal mount; on complete → PI → succeeded\n  - Webhook arrives | DB Order.status = 'paid'; SSE pushes to active frontend session\n  - Tab re-entry after close | GET /checkout-session → restore step + PI status; re-render correct UI\n  - Card decline | PI.lastPaymentError populated; FSM → requires_payment_method; user can retry\n\n- Section links to answers-html/03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.html and answers-html/04-real-time-updates-webhooks.html\n\n### ④ API Design / BFF\n- Protocol choice table (Pattern | Use in payments | Why):\n  - REST/HTTPS | Cart CRUD, session management, PaymentIntent confirm, order fetch | Idempotency-Key header; standard error taxonomy; caching for GET\n  - SSE | Payment status push after confirmation | Server→client push; no polling; AbortController cancel; works with standard auth cookies\n  - postMessage | Stripe Elements iframe → parent page | Cross-origin card data isolation — PCI requirement\n  - WebSocket | Live dashboard (multi-concurrent payments) | Full-duplex for high-frequency event push; not needed for single-session checkout\n  - Polling (fallback) | Payment status if SSE unavailable | Exponential backoff; safe fallback for restrictive network proxies\n\n- Core endpoints table (Method | Endpoint | Purpose):\n  - POST | /checkout/session | Create or resume CheckoutSession; returns sessionId + step\n  - PATCH | /checkout/session/:id/step | Advance to next step (validates current step server-side)\n  - POST | /payment-intents | Create PI server-side; returns clientSecret (never stored, used once)\n  - POST | /payment-intents/:id/confirm | Trigger confirmCardPayment; idempotent via Idempotency-Key\n  - GET | /payment-intents/:id/status | Poll fallback for PI status\n  - GET | /payment-status-stream?piId=:id | SSE stream for real-time PI status updates\n  - POST | /webhooks/stripe | Verify Stripe-Signature; update Order; push to SSE clients\n  - GET | /orders/:id | Confirmation page data fetch\n\n- Streaming / async lifecycle:\n  ```\n  User clicks Pay →\n    [1] POST /payment-intents/confirm (Idempotency-Key: session.idempotencyKey)\n    [2] BFF calls stripe.paymentIntents.confirm()\n    [3] If 3DS required: return nextAction to frontend → render ThreeDSModal\n    [4] After 3DS: PI status = processing → SSE pushes update\n    [5] Stripe webhook → BFF verifies sig → updates Order → SSE broadcast → UI → ConfirmationPage\n  ```\n\n- Network lifecycle notes:\n  - Idempotency: rotate key per attempt; safe to retry POST on timeout without double-charge\n  - Cancel: if user navigates away during processing, Order status resolved by webhook (frontend re-reads on return)\n  - 3DS redirect recovery: store PI id in sessionStorage before redirect; restore on return\n  - Backoff: poll fallback at 1s, 2s, 4s, 8s (cap 30s); show \"still processing...\" after 10s\n\n- Section links to answers-html/04-real-time-updates-webhooks.html and answers-html/06-error-handling-resilience.html\n\n### ⑤ Deep Dive — 5 tabs\nOpening line (in prose): \"I'll lead with Security (PCI/iframe model) and Resilience — happy to switch to Performance or i18n if you prefer.\"\n\n**Tab: Security** (id=\"panel-sec\", active by default)\n- PCI scope: Stripe Elements = SAQ-A; card data never in our DOM, memory, or server logs\n- iframe isolation: Stripe renders CardNumberElement in cross-origin iframe on js.stripe.com; postMessage only exchanges tokens (pm_xxx), never PANs\n- CSP: `frame-src https://js.stripe.com https://hooks.stripe.com; script-src 'self' https://js.stripe.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.stripe.com`\n- clientSecret: keep in memory only (not localStorage, not URL params); expires after PI use; rotate idempotency key per attempt\n- Clickjacking: X-Frame-Options DENY on checkout page + frame-ancestors 'none' in CSP; Stripe iframe is explicitly allowed via frame-src, not by weakening our own page framing policy\n- 3DS: iframe modal challenge or redirect; validate redirect return params server-side via webhook; never trust client-side redirect_status alone\n\n**Tab: Performance** (id=\"panel-perf\")\n- Stripe.js: load on every page (Stripe recommends this for fraud signals); use &lt;script async&gt; + preconnect to js.stripe.com\n- CLS prevention: reserve fixed height (e.g. 48px) for Elements iframe mount container; don't let it reflow surrounding content\n- Bundle split: core checkout critical path is &lt;60KB; defer Stripe.js (already async); lazy-load Apple/Google Pay button SDKs only when available\n- TBT: move heavy Stripe SDK work off main thread by loading async; INP-safe by debouncing BIN detection to 300ms\n- One-click checkout: preload PI on product page hover/intent; preconnect Stripe on page load; so that \"Pay\" click triggers confirm only, not create+confirm\n- LCP: inline critical CSS; preload hero product image; SSR order summary so content is above-fold on first byte\n\n**Tab: Resilience** (id=\"panel-res\")\n- Idempotency: every POST /payment-intents/confirm carries Idempotency-Key from sessionStorage; safe to retry on network timeout\n- 3DS redirect recovery: stash PI id + step in sessionStorage before redirect; restore on return to correct UI state\n- Offline detection: navigator.onLine + online/offline events; show \"you're offline, your cart is saved\" banner; queue retry on reconnect\n- Webhook ground truth: never trust only client-side PI status; always wait for webhook-confirmed Order.status before showing success\n- Circuit breaker: after 3 consecutive 5xx from /payment-intents/confirm in 60s, show \"payment system temporarily unavailable\" with retry-after countdown; don't let user hammer degraded backend\n- Tab re-entry: GET /checkout-session on tab focus to reconcile FSM state with server PI status; BroadcastChannel for multi-tab same cart conflict detection\n\n**Tab: Observability** (id=\"panel-obs\")\n- Funnel events: checkout_started, step_completed (step, duration_ms), payment_form_engaged, pay_button_clicked, payment_succeeded / payment_failed (decline_code, attempt_number)\n- PCI-safe sanitization: Sentry beforeSend strips card_number, cvv, full_name from breadcrumbs; analytics allowlist only (pi_id hashed, decline_code, country)\n- Performance marks: performance.mark('stripe-js-start') before script inject → performance.mark('stripe-js-ready') in Stripe onReady callback; performance.mark('elements-mounted') in Elements onChange\n- Real-time dashboard: payment_success_rate (1m rolling window), decline_rate by code, 3DS completion %, Stripe.js p95 load time; alert if success_rate &lt; 90% for 5 min\n- Deploy regression: correlate deploy timestamp with Sentry error spike and Datadog payment_failed rate; cross-check Stripe Dashboard for PSP-side failures vs. our API errors\n\n**Tab: i18n** (id=\"panel-i18n\")\n- Currency formatting: Intl.NumberFormat(locale, {style:'currency', currency}) for display; always store/transmit in minor units (integer cents); special-case JPY (0 decimals), KWD (3 decimals)\n- Tax display: server provides {amount, taxIncluded: boolean, taxAmount}; component renders \"incl. VAT\" or \"+ tax\" based on flag; never derive tax from frontend\n- RTL: CSS logical properties (margin-inline-start not margin-left); card number field kept LTR via dir=\"ltr\" on the input; CVV icon flips position; error messages align-start\n- Local payment methods: server returns ranked PaymentMethod[] for locale; frontend renders in server order; each method has {type, displayName, logoUrl, flow: 'redirect'|'iframe'|'async'}; iDEAL/BLIK are redirect; Pix/UPI are async (polling for QR scan); konbini is async + shows convenience store selector\n- Server error translation: decline codes mapped to i18n key in frontend dictionary; fallback to generic \"payment_failed\" if code unknown; never show raw PSP error strings to users\n\n### Interview close (30 sec)\ncallout: \"Three patterns I'd repeat: (1) card data stays in Stripe's iframe — scope our PCI to SAQ-A and never touch raw PANs; (2) idempotency keys + webhook ground truth — rotate per attempt, never trust client-side confirmCardPayment alone; (3) PaymentIntent as FSM — model status transitions explicitly so every UI state is deterministic and recoverable.\"\n\n- Section links: answers-html/06-error-handling-resilience.html, answers-html/02-payment-security-pci-compliance.html, answers-html/08-observability-analytics.html\n\n## Nav and footer links\n- Nav title: \"Payments SD — Interview\"\n- Nav links: #requirements #architecture #data-model #api-design #deep-dive\n- Top-right links: href=\"../payments-system-frontend-architecture.html\" and href=\"answers-html/index.html\"\n- Footer: links to answers-html/index.html, payments-system-frontend-architecture.html, payments-system-design-doc.md\n\n## HTML rules\n- NO data-demo panels\n- Mermaid: startOnLoad: false; lazy render via mermaid.run()\n- Deep tabs default: Security active (not Performance like in the reference)\n- Checklist persistence via localStorage (same pattern as reference)\n- Copy exact JS for collapse, nav observer, deep tabs, checklist from reference file\n\nWrite the full HTML file now. It should be self-contained, ~700-900 lines, match the reference's visual style exactly."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_012xinWFsdPnoxwdALhuwTqE","session_id":"f24c5cdf-0369-4a81-99d5-ba16ab3babb1","uuid":"6c77a7fa-4ccb-4aa7-a226-59268b9e222f","timestamp":"2026-06-20T19:53:58.286Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write payments-system-system-design-interview.html"}
