{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01CwNGe8gaD2XdFGFQ8i4GQV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t2026-06-20 | scaffold | created /Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system\n2\t2026-06-20 | design-doc | wrote payments-system-design-doc.md — 9 sections, 90+ questions covering checkout UX, PCI/security, state management, real-time updates, performance, error handling, i18n, observability, provider abstraction\n3\t2026-06-20 | gen-plan | 9 answer tasks\n4\t2026-06-21 | answers/01 | wrote 01-checkout-flow-form-ux.md — 10 answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) covering multi-step flow state machine, card masking/BIN detection, validation timing, address autocomplete, loading states, order summary sync, progressive disclosure, saved payment handoff, config-driven fields, smart retry UX\n5\t2026-06-21 | answers/02 | wrote 02-payment-security-pci-compliance.md — 10 answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) covering PCI DSS scope/SAQ tiers, Stripe Elements postMessage mechanism, cross-origin iframe styling, CSP directives, tokenization lifecycle, client secret storage risks, clickjacking defense, custom fonts in iframes, pen-tester client secret evaluation, legacy-to-Stripe migration strategy\n6\t2026-06-21 | answers/03 | wrote 03-state-management-transaction-lifecycle.md — 10 answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) covering PaymentIntent FSM/UI rendering, idempotency keys, optimistic UI limits, multi-step form persistence, tab-close re-entry recovery, concurrent tab conflicts via BroadcastChannel, ad-blocker redirect fallback, soft-decline retry loop, XState machine definition, and WebView postMessage bridge architecture\n7\t2026-06-21 | answers/04 | wrote 04-real-time-updates-webhooks.md — 10 answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) covering confirmCardPayment vs webhook ground truth reconciliation, SSE/WebSocket/polling comparison, exponential backoff polling implementation, client-side attack scenario for frontend-only success detection, processing state UX for async payment methods, re-surfacing outcomes after navigation, webhook-vs-UI conflict resolution, multi-context SSE notification system, webhook-to-frontend consistency pipeline, and POS dashboard WebSocket normalization with render optimization\n8\t2026-06-21 | answers/05 | wrote 05-performance-core-web-vitals.md — 10 answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) covering Stripe.js every-page loading strategy, CLS prevention for Elements iframe mount, bundle-splitting critical path, TBT/INP impact of payment SDKs, TTI optimization via parallel server fetches, resource hints (preconnect/preload) for Stripe/Fonts/CDN, SSR vs SSG vs CSR tradeoffs, 3G LCP audit playbook, network connection sequence for Elements iframe, and one-click checkout < 2s performance architecture\n9\t2026-06-21 | answers/06 | wrote 06-error-handling-resilience.md — 10 answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) covering error taxonomy/classifyStripeError dispatch, decline code allowlist/denylist pattern (stolen_card anti-enumeration), 3DS challenge flow with sequence diagram, network timeout vs definitive failure ambiguity, Stripe.js load-failure graceful fallback, frontend circuit breaker with closed/open/half-open states, last-step server error UX preservation, full 3DS2 architecture with redirect recovery across React state, offline resilience with idempotency queuing and navigator.onLine limits, and cross-origin Stripe iframe error diagnosis strategy\n10\t2026-06-21 | answers/07 | wrote 07-internationalization-localization.md — 10 answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) covering Intl.NumberFormat minor-unit currency formatting, tax-inclusive vs exclusive display data contracts, RTL checkout challenges (card number LTR pinning, CVV icon orientation, CSS logical properties), data-driven local payment method selector (iDEAL/BLIK/Pix/UPI flows), locale-safe date formatting for expiry/invoice/delivery, server error message translation via decline code map, multi-currency marketplace display, Japan expansion (konbini async flow, reversed address schema, locale-driven form), robust currency utility module with zero/3-decimal handling, and global payment method ranking with graceful degradation\n11\t2026-06-21 | answers/08 | wrote 08-observability-analytics.md — 10 answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) covering checkout funnel event taxonomy with typed envelope, three-tier abandonment classification with Beacon API, four-layer PCI sanitization strategy (Sentry beforeSend/Datadog RUM mask/analytics allowlist), custom performance.mark RUM instrumentation for Stripe.js init and Elements mount, real-time success rate dashboard with Datadog monitor YAML, retry effectiveness instrumentation with soft/hard decline segmentation, payment_intent_id risk framework with SHA-256 hashing alternative, full A/B experiment design for load-time vs abandonment causality, 60-second incident detection observability architecture, and deploy-regression diagnostic playbook with Datadog/Sentry/Stripe Dashboard\n12\t2026-06-21 | answers/09 | wrote 09-architecture-provider-abstraction.md — 10 answers (7 Core + 3 Deep) covering IPaymentProvider adapter pattern, PSP SDK normalisation (Stripe/Adyen/Braintree), PSP-agnostic payment method config data model, redirect vs iframe auth flow abstraction, thin-shim vs rich-unified-API tradeoffs, error normalisation to FrontendPaymentError categories, lazy SDK loading with registry + dynamic import, multi-PSP DOM mounting with visibility toggling and event bus, provider failover architecture constraints (pre-created server tokens, double-charge risk, card iframe limitation), and Braintree→Stripe migration playbook (deterministic cohort routing, parallel SDK chunking, cross-provider analytics, migration-complete criteria)\n13\t2026-06-21 | architecture-map | wrote payments-system-frontend-architecture.html — 21 nodes across 7 layers, 38 edges, 5 flow walkthroughs (checkout, decline/retry, 3DS, async payment, PSP failover), 9 sections mapped to answer pages\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"